{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1359978-fsa-citizenship-currency-questions","id":1359978,"title":"FSA Citizenship & Currency Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-09T15:13:24-08:00","id":1359978,"title":"FSA Citizenship & Currency Questions","content":"1). Why does the FSA use the yen symbol instead of the dollar sign? Maybe the government wanted to distinguish themselves from the old USA and figured the new symbol wouldn't get confused for the money of the isolationist Nipponese?<br /> <br /> 2). Is FSA currency still called the dollar despite the new symbol, or did it change to yen or something else?<br /> <br /> 3). You need to pay 10k in taxes to get a single vote, but you don't get first-class citizenship until you pay 30k. Does this mean people who aren't first-class citizens can still vote by paying enough taxes?<br /> <br /> 4). You're a second-class citizen if either parent is a first-class citizen. Is that the only way to become a second-class citizen? Based on the previous question, if you pay 10k in taxes, are you a second-class citizen despite lacking a first-class citizen parent, or are you a non-citizen who can - possibly - vote? I can see the government letting people have second-class citizenship by paying 10k as a way of increasing revenue, since otherwise nobody'd bother paying 10k-29k.<br /> <br /> 5). Given that citizenship is a matter of paying taxes, is it common for wealthy foreigners to pay 30k in taxes before visiting as a safety precaution, or do foreign visitors get special legal protections via international law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 01-09-2020, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T15:35:06-08:00","id":1359985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1359978-fsa-citizenship-currency-questions#post1359978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1). Why does the FSA use the yen symbol instead of the dollar sign? Maybe the government wanted to distinguish themselves from the old USA and figured the new symbol wouldn't get confused for t he money of the isolationist Nipponese?<br /> <br /> 2). Is FSA currency still called the dollar despite the new symbol, or did it change to yen or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you seeing this? As far as I know, the currency of Nippon is still the Yen and that of the FSA is the Dollar. Otherwise, maybe the currency of the world is the Yen because Nippon is the most overtly powerful/advanced nation now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1359978-fsa-citizenship-currency-questions#post1359978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3). You need to pay 10k in taxes to get a single vote, but you don't get first-class citizenship until you pay 30k. Does this mean people who aren't first-class citizens can still vote by paying enough taxes?<br /> <br /> 4). You're a second-class citizen if either parent is a first-class citizen. Is that the only way to become a second-class citizen? Based on the previous question, if you pay 10k in taxes, are you a second-class citizen despite lacking a first-class citizen parent, or are you a non-citizen who can - possibly -vote? I can see the government letting people have second-class citizenship by paying 10k as a way of increasing revenue, since otherwise nobody'd bother paying 10k-29k.<br /> <br /> 5). Given that citizenship is a matter of paying taxes, is it common for wealthy foreigners to pay 30k in taxes before visiting as a safety precaution, or do foreign visitors get special legal protections via international law?</div> </div> </div> </div>3) I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> 4) Given the citizenship seems to be financially based, that seems reasonable. I'd assume that to keep your citizenship you have to keep paying your taxes.<br /> <br /> 5) Presumably diplomats get the protections they've always had. As for others, figure it's a case by case basis designed to squeeze as much money as possible out of potential foreign citizens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:07:44-08:00","id":1360015,"title":"","content":"I thought the base currency of the world was the yuan from China.<br /> <br /> Thats not saying it\u2019s the world\u2019s currency. I mean it\u2019s like the dollar today. I\u2019m saying the dollar has been replaced as the currency others are measured against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:51:30-08:00","id":1360021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1359978-fsa-citizenship-currency-questions?p=1360015#post1360015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the base currency of the world was the yuan from China.<br /> <br /> Thats not saying it\u2019s the world\u2019s currency. I mean it\u2019s like the dollar today. I\u2019m saying the dollar has been replaced as the currency others are measured against.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a more sensible take on the issue. While Nippon is probably overall the most technologically advanced, it's also only recently rejoined the public stage and is still quite isolated in terms of allowing visitors/trade/etc. China basically saved the world from the Aberrants back in 2060 and seems to be the most powerful nation in the Aeon era. Figure it's currency would be the measure against which others are compared.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, figure for the OPs 1) and 2) the FSA is using the Yuan symbol instead of the Yen one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:59:27-08:00","id":1360023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1359978-fsa-citizenship-currency-questions?p=1359985#post1359985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you seeing this? As far as I know, the currency of Nippon is still the Yen and that of the FSA is the Dollar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity Continuum: Aeon, page 58, near the top of the second column. It states that every 10,000 gets you a vote, and uses a yen symbol instead of a dollar sign. An internet search on global currency indicates the yen is a Y with two horizontal lines while the yuan is a Y with one horizontal line, so the book is definitely using the yen. So either someone made a really weird typographical mistake, or something even weirder happened to America's currency in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T19:41:39-08:00","id":1360032,"title":"","content":"In the old setting, I may be wrong, but I think the oficial international money was New Yuan, but not sure about the siymbol they used before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T19:59:10-08:00","id":1360034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1359978-fsa-citizenship-currency-questions?p=1360023#post1360023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trinity Continuum: Aeon, page 58, near the top of the second column. It states that every 10,000 gets you a vote, and uses a yen symbol instead of a dollar sign. An internet search on global currency indicates the yen is a Y with two horizontal lines while the yuan is a Y with one horizontal line, so the book is definitely using the yen. So either someone made a really weird typographical mistake, or something even weirder happened to America's currency in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd lean toward typographical mistake or just actual mistake. Until you mentioned it I didn't know the notations for the yen and yuan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}